>I gave a white unicorn an amethist (sp) and got the message - the 
>unicorn hesitantly accepts your gift? What does this mean - also 
>are there different results for giving gems to different color
>unicorns. And last but not least what are the horns good for (besides
>being healed when they are applied... - boy they must be worth a lot
>to loose the luck you do when you kill a unicorn ..


  Well, it's a little bit complicated . . ..  If you throw an
_identified_ jewel to a co-aligned unicorn (i.e. a white unicorn
if you are lawful, gray if you are neutral, etc.), your luck
increases by 5.  On the other hand, if you throw an identified
jewel to a NON-co-aligned unicorn, your luck changes randomly
by anything from -3 to +3; that's what happened to you.

  Your luck increases by 1 if you throw an unidentified jewel to
any unicorn, co-aligned or not.  Throwing an identified worthless
piece of glass to a unicorn is simply a waste of time.

  Killing a co-aligned unicorn decreases your luck by 5, but killing
a non-co-aligned unicorn does not change your luck, and actually
improves your alignment (with your god).

  Unicorn horns are useful for fixing a number of problems, especially
when they are blessed.

